---
description: TickTickSync Abyss fork — process that analyst, developer, and tester agents follow.
alwaysApply: true
---

Follow DEV_FLOW.md at the repo root.

- Pilot gate phases and issue handoff: `.cursor/rules/pilot-results.mdc` (results under `docs/pilot/results/`).
- Case ID and expected behavior in ABYSS_FIRST_CASES.md (or PO_STATUS.md for an open bug) before the code change.
- Failing test named by that ID, then the fix. Do not delete or weaken tests to go green.
- `npx vitest run` and `npm run build` must pass, including the synchronizationInner integration test.
- Update canonical docs in the same PR. Archive docs (GTD_SYNC_*, TT_ABYSS_ROADMAP, SYNC_PROJECTS_AND_SUBTASKS) are not requirements.
- Every PR that changes behavior updates TEST_PLAN.md in that same PR (steps, expected result, pilot status). Reject a PR that does not.
- Branch and pull request into abyss-mapping only. Do not push abyss-mapping or master, do not merge, do not tag.
- Pilot vault only. No secrets or personal absolute paths. Do not invent live-vault results.
